{
  "id": "recursive-model",
  "term": "recursive model",
  "definition": "In this learning context, a recursive model is a formal way of representing hyperbolic reward discounting step by step over time, as in the hyperbolically discounted temporal difference model. Unlike a parallel model that adds up separately discounted rewards, it allows later rewards in a sequence to interact nonlinearly with earlier ones.",
